Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), librsvg2-bin, python3-pil
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tolome-gdm-theme
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell-common, libglib2.0-bin, libglib2.0-dev-bin, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Tolome background for the GDM login screen
 Gives the GDM login screen a darkened, blurred Ganvié background (or a flat
 indigo, or the original GNOME look) without modifying files of other
 packages: the theme of GNOME Shell (gnome-shell-theme.gresource) is diverted
 with dpkg-divert and regenerated from the original by a trigger, so the
 background survives GNOME updates.
 .
 The mode is set in /etc/tolome/gdm-background.conf (image, flat or off).
 Removing the package restores the original theme.
